-- Q13 [Muscle Mechanics & Contraction Dynamics] medium skill2 ans=B
WITH q AS (
  INSERT INTO questions (section, topic, subtopic, question_text, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, foundation, content_category, discipline, cognitive_skill, estimated_time_seconds)
  VALUES ('bio_biochem', 'The Musculoskeletal System', 'Muscle Mechanics & Contraction Dynamics', 'A weightlifter switches from holding a light dumbbell to lifting a much heavier one, and the biceps brachii must generate substantially greater force. To grade up the muscle''s force for the heavier load, the nervous system most directly recruits which type of motor units?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "Smaller motor units with lower-threshold motor neurons"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Larger motor units with higher-threshold motor neurons"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Larger motor units with lower-threshold motor neurons"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Smaller motor units with higher-threshold motor neurons"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'This is a Biology question that falls under the content category ''Organ Systems.'' The answer is B because increasing whole-muscle force requires recruiting larger motor units, which are driven by bigger, higher-threshold motor neurons. As the textbook states, smaller motor units have smaller, lower-threshold motor neurons that are more excitable and fire first, producing only a small degree of contractile strength; "As more strength is needed, larger motor units, with bigger, higher-threshold motor neurons are enlisted to activate larger muscle fibers," a process called recruitment that makes the contraction progressively stronger (lines 17652-17657). The book uses this exact biceps brachii example: minimal force lets the muscle pick up a feather, whereas recruiting the largest motor units lets "a heavy weight to be lifted by the same muscle" (lines 17659-17660). (Choice A) is wrong: smaller, lower-threshold motor units are recruited first and generate only "a relatively small degree of contractile strength," so leaning on them cannot meet the demand of a heavier load (lines 17652-17654). (Choice B) is correct: lifting a heavier load enlists the larger, higher-threshold motor units last and adds the most force, since the largest units can generate up to 50 times the force of the smallest (lines 17655-17658). (Choice C) couples the correct unit size with the wrong neuron threshold; larger motor units are governed by higher-threshold, not lower-threshold, motor neurons (lines 17655-17656). (Choice D) reverses both attributes relative to the muscle fiber size they activate, since higher-threshold neurons supply the larger, not smaller, motor units (lines 17646-17656). This is a Knowledge of Scientific Concepts and Principles question because you must recall how the nervous system uses recruitment of larger, higher-threshold motor units to increase whole-muscle force.', 'medium', '3B', 'Organ Systems', 'biology', 2, 100)
  RETURNING id
)
